s10-7-p8 : Block
s10-7-p8 = prose (cons "Suppose every event has a stable authenticated identifier, the ledger atomically records applied identifiers before acknowledging them, and the new version can decode every event that may be routed to it. Installing changes no ledger entry. **Routing new admissions to \(v_1\) occurs before draining**: the routing transition forbids creation of further \(v_0\)-owned obligations while preserving the assignment of existing old-version work. Draining applies the idempotent ledger transition; retirement is enabled only when no route, active frame, queued delivery, or in-flight request still refers to \(v_0\). Induction over these four transition constructors preserves the at-most-once ledger invariant, including the mixed-version interval." nil)
